A||N||9||Lance||Informal Fiero get together in Midwest?||||14||
Z||000000||Lance||02-12-2000||10:09 AM||||I think it would be great if some of us Fiero owners from the Midwest (Kansas, Missouri, Nebraska, ect...) could get together this spring. How does someone make an official Fiero Club? I think we need one in this area. What do you think?||||reg||14
Z||000001||deceler8||02-12-2000||01:19 PM||||Midwest Fiero Club will be having a meeting of the membership on Saturday, March 18 at 2:00 pm. The clubhouse is located in Onawa, Iowa (about 60 mi. north of Omaha on I-29).<P>The absolute nicest gathering place for a car club that I've ever seen. <P>If you want more info, contact Paul Duff at duff@willinet.net and I'm sure he'll get back to you.<P>As I understand, folks come from all over the Midwest to attend the meetings. ||||reg||10
Z||000002||sluppy123||02-12-2000||02:44 PM||||Deceler8-Do you plan on attending the meeting on the 18th. I haven't decided if i'm Going or not. <P>-Brian||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||02-12-2000||06:01 PM||||I think Lance was hoping for something closer to the Kansas City area. I'm game Lance, let's see how much interest there is and try to plan something informal when the weather gets nicer. It'd be cool to have 4-6 Fieros all lined up in a Pizza Hut parking lot while we sit around swapping lies or something like that. Maybe even go for a short cruise and take some pics. Although, the Midwest Fiero Club meeting sounds like it might be fun too.||||reg||1
Z||000004||deceler8||02-13-2000||02:12 PM||||Yes, I intend to be there on the 18th. This will be the first meeting I have attended (just joined in October). <P>They'll be discussing the events planned for the coming summer and I know several of the members are planning to go to the national event in Louisville (I believe) in late june.<P>As I understand it, there is a group affiliated with Midwest Fieros that meet in Jeff City, MO, but I don't know any more than that. And Jeff isn't exactly close to KC either.||||reg||10
Z||000005||Lance||02-13-2000||02:55 PM||||Yea, I think I am going to the midwest meet. That sounds like a good time. I also would like to do something in this area. Just to see other people's Fieros. I saw one other Fiero last night at a gas station. That was the only Fiero I've seen in the area (Kansas City). It was nice. I'm sure there are others. ||||reg||10
Z||000006||RICK||02-14-2000||08:05 PM||||Lance, welcome to the forum, now your the 2nd person I know from Missouri.  I thought I was out here all alone.  BTW I'm from St. Louis out by Six-Flags on 44.  There is a small club here in St. Louis, I forgot when the date is but it is in the spring.  Once I find out I'll post it.||||reg||10
Z||000007||Bugsy||02-16-2000||01:57 PM||||i'd love to attend a midwest get together...problem is i work weekends, as a result i have yet to join the midwest fieros car club but Paul and Jolene Duff turned me on to a fellow enthusiast in Louisville NE. he is gonna do the necessary bodywork on my go-cart next month. I did drive the fiero from Lincoln, NE to Overland Park KS last Sunday, big computer expo at the Trade Center.ever tried to pack $1000 worth of computer pieces parts in a Fiero...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Bugsy (edited 02-16-2000).]||||reg||6
